    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive engine is headlined by **Lawrence Butler** (65.41) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (64.07). **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+10%) and a strong platoon advantage against Soriano, positioning him as our premier outfield play. Meanwhile, **Geraldo Perdomo** continues to hold elite value, buoyed by a favorable matchup against Prielipp and a secondary lineup boost that keeps his efficiency score well into the strong category. **Taylor Ward** (63.85) and **Tyler Freeman** (63.78) also command high confidence; **Taylor Ward** thrives on the Roki Sasaki matchup, as the wind conditions and potential leadoff spot mitigate the platoon disadvantage, while **Tyler Freeman** capitalizes on an advantageous park and a favorable setup despite the risk posed by the opposing catcher\u2019s pop time.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision was sitting **Drew Gilbert** (37.09), who fell just shy of our 40.0 baseline floor. Despite the potential, he is hampered by a poor park factor and the presence of Bachar on the mound, keeping him below the threshold required to justify burning a game cap. Conversely, we are keeping **Gavin Sheets** (41.13) in the lineup for now, though his status remains volatile; he is surviving primarily on his dynamic platoon edge, but facing an elite arm like deGrom severely limits his ceiling and makes him the most likely candidate to be swapped should official lineups reveal a deeper batting order slot.\n\nRisk management remains a primary theme for LawDog today, particularly with our \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Jeremiah Jackson** and **Taylor Ward**. While the favorable wind conditions at the park provide a solid floor against Roki Sasaki, these scores are projections contingent on specific spots in the order. If **Jeremiah Jackson** or **Taylor Ward** are shifted lower in the lineup, their efficiency will plummet. We are also monitoring the health of our depth chart, as **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Daulton Varsho** remain sidelined on the IL, leaving us reliant on the current active roster to maintain our competitive edge in the scarcity-driven stolen base category.",
